Path tracing in Advanced Video Options: a list of None, Real Time and Reference that sets
d3d12_PathTracing, XRenderD3D12's lighting of the opaque surfaces by paths (DXR 1.1) in place of the
light maps and the ambient light, in the last row of the right column, under HDR output. Choosing it
while HDR is None sets HDR to Soft (the path tracer needs the HDR pipeline); greyed out with another
renderer or a graphics card without ray tracing. Written against VideoAdv.lua as
04-video-ray-tracing.patch leaves it (Patch Scripts.cmd applies the patches in the order of their
numbers) and applied by Patch Scripts.cmd to FCData/Scripts.pak.

